# Windows: Fully Isolated Java + Gradle Setup

## Project Layout

```text
my-project/
│
├── .tools/
│   └── jdk-21/
│       ├── bin/
│       ├── lib/
│       └── ...
│
├── gradlew
├── gradlew.bat
├── gradle/
│   └── wrapper/
│       ├── gradle-wrapper.jar
│       └── gradle-wrapper.properties
│
├── build.gradle
└── settings.gradle
```

---

## Step 1: Download a Portable JDK

Download a ZIP distribution (not an installer) of your preferred JDK.

Good choices:

- Eclipse Adoptium (Temurin)
- Amazon (Corretto)
- Oracle Corporation (Oracle JDK)

Extract it into:

```text
my-project\.tools\jdk-21\
```

Verify that this exists:

```text
my-project\.tools\jdk-21\bin\java.exe
my-project\.tools\jdk-21\bin\javac.exe
```

---

## Step 2: Generate the Gradle Wrapper

If the project does not already contain a wrapper, generate one once:

```cmd
gradle wrapper
```

Commit these files:

```text
gradlew
gradlew.bat
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
```

After that, nobody needs a global Gradle installation.

---

## Step 3: Build Using the Local JDK

### Command Prompt (cmd.exe)

```cmd
set JAVA_HOME=%CD%\.tools\jdk-21
set PATH=%JAVA_HOME%\bin;%PATH%

gradlew.bat build
```

### PowerShell

```powershell
$env:JAVA_HOME="$PWD\.tools\jdk-21"
$env:PATH="$env:JAVA_HOME\bin;$env:PATH"

.\gradlew.bat build
```

---

## Step 4: One-Click Build Script

Create `build-local.cmd`:

```cmd
@echo off

set JAVA_HOME=%~dp0.tools\jdk-21
set PATH=%JAVA_HOME%\bin;%PATH%

call "%~dp0gradlew.bat" build
```

Run:

```cmd
build-local.cmd
```

---

## Optional: Verify Isolation

Check which Java is being used:

```cmd
gradlew.bat -version
```

The output should show:

```text
JVM: 21 (...)
Java Home: C:\...\my-project\.tools\jdk-21
```

If the Java Home points inside your project folder, the build is completely isolated from any system-installed JDK.

---

## Cleanup

To remove everything:

```text
Delete:
- my-project/
```

This removes:

- The JDK
- The Gradle wrapper files
- The build outputs

The only remaining Gradle files may be in:

```text
%USERPROFILE%\.gradle
```

If you want _absolute_ isolation with no use of the global Gradle cache at all, Gradle can also be configured to use a project-local `.gradle-cache` directory.
